I have updated the animation plans for sections 2, 4, and 5 to ensure a one-to-one mapping with the lecture lines and to improve visual storytelling. 

- **Section 2 (Span)**: Revised animations to show the transition from a 2D span (non-parallel vectors) to a 1D span (parallel vectors), matching the lecture's conclusion about being "stuck" in a line.
- **Section 4 (Linear Independence)**: Streamlined to 3 animation steps to match the 3 lecture lines, focusing on how each vector adds a unique dimension.
- **Section 5 (Basis)**: Expanded to 5 animation steps to match the 5 lecture lines, demonstrating both independence and complete span using unit vectors and coordinate grids.

The animations use hexadecimal colors and focus on clear, native Manim-style visualizations (scaling, rotating, pulsing, grid overlays) without requiring 3D methods or external assets.

```json
{
  "section_2": {
    "animations": [
      "Create vector u (#98FB98) and vector v (#FF6347) at origin.",
      "Show u and v scaling and stretching to cover the plane.",
      "Fill the background with a faint grey grid (#A9A9A9).",
      "Rotate vector v until it overlaps perfectly with vector u.",
      "The grid disappears, leaving only one bright white line (#FFFFFF)."
    ]
  },
  "section_4": {
    "animations": [
      "Create vector p (#7B68EE) and its 1D line span (#7B68EE).",
      "Add vector q (#FFDAB9) and expand the span to a 2D plane (#A9A9A9).",
      "Pulse p and q together in white (#FFFFFF) to highlight the set."
    ]
  },
  "section_5": {
    "animations": [
      "Display unit vectors i (#F0E68C) and j (#E6E6FA) at origin.",
      "Pulse i and j in white (#FFFFFF) to show they are independent.",
      "Overlay a coordinate grid (#333333) covering the entire screen.",
      "Show i and j scaling to reach a specific target point (#FFFFFF).",
      "Highlight both vectors and label them as \"Basis\" in gold (#FFD700)."
    ]
  }
}
```
